# appowners.env - the appowners settings, as a split box keeps them in /etc/cti-agent/fleet.d/appowners.env.
# Generated by scripts/lanes from fleet.env.example and settings.manifest: edit those.
# Lines starting with # are optional; set the others. Secrets are not here:
# store each with `sudo cti-agent-secrets set NAME` (cti-agent-onboard does it for you).

# The security team, copied on EVERY application owner email (run-appowners,
# cti-mailer --lane owner), so it sees what each owner was sent. Not the same
# list as WAS_TO: WAS_TO is the AppSec weekly's audience and can be wider.
# Each address must be at a domain the owner lane allows (fleet-owners domain
# list), exactly like a watcher; one that is not is left off and logged, and
# the owner email still goes. Unset means no copy. A plain list - no $NAME:
#
#     WAS_OWNER_CC=security@example.com,appsec-lead@example.com
#WAS_OWNER_CC=
